+comes to rest at the stop point of a zone it has not been granted (the leg is
+re-timed, its path is unchanged), and releases a zone once its MEASURED position is
+past the exit. Without a configured PLC (the cell's robots.yaml ``vass:`` block or
+``UMARELL_VASS_CONNECT``) the port is ignored and the tree runs exactly as before,
+unless the tree or the cell sets ``required`` (then: ``vass_unavailable``).
+Under ``LOCKSTEP=1`` an ompl-compound step's legs (``sync_group``) are never held
+in motion (that would be ``lockstep_lost``): their tables carry no zone inside the
+step, and each such leg takes the grants of the zones it enters at rest, at its
+start, before the barrier, then runs exactly as planned. A table derived for the
+other lockstep setting is refused before anything moves (``vass_lockstep_mismatch``).
 
